=== WHAT THIS PROVES ===
The per-channel scale in the int8 weight-only matmul is VERIFIED, not cosmetic. With the
CORRECT scale the int8 output passes the quantization-aware golden (cosine >= 0.99,
max_rel_err <= 5e-2, pcc >= 0.99); with a WRONG per-channel scale the SAME int8 dequant-matmul
FAILS the golden on ALL THREE relaxed metrics, decisively. So a scale bug cannot slip through
the gate — the test is sensitive to per-channel scale correctness.

=== THE CORRUPTION ===
quantize_per_channel(W) -> (wq int8[K,N], scale fp32[N])  (correct per-output-channel scale)
scale_wrong = scale * linspace(0.25, 4.0, N)              (a wrong gain ramped across channels)
The int8 weights wq are UNCHANGED; only the per-channel dequant scale is wrong, so each output
column n is multiplied by the wrong factor scale_wrong[n] instead of scale[n].

=== STANDALONE EVIDENCE (quant_golden + metrics, verbatim) ===
correct scale  : cosine=1.00000 max_rel_err=0.0000 pcc=1.00000
wrong scale    : cosine=0.88796 max_rel_err=3.0000 pcc=0.88796
assert_quant_correct(correct) -> PASS
assert_quant_correct(wrong)   -> FAIL (quant assert_quant_correct FAILED: cosine=0.887963 (need >= 0.99), max_rel_err=3...)

