=== WHY IT FAILS ON ALL THREE METRICS ===
- cosine 0.888 < 0.99 : the per-channel gain ramp re-weights columns differently, rotating the
  output vector away from the reference (cosine is scale-invariant only for a UNIFORM factor;
  a per-channel ramp breaks the direction).
- max_rel_err 3.0 >> 5e-2 : columns scaled up to 4x / down to 0.25x diverge element-wise.
- pcc 0.888 < 0.99 : the per-column correlation collapses for the same reason.
- bit_exact 0.0 : no output element survives the wrong dequant.
(A UNIFORM wrong scale, e.g. scale*2, would fail on max_rel_err alone with cosine ~1.0; the
ramp is used here precisely because it is a decisive, structurally-wrong PER-CHANNEL error.)

=== RESULT ===
The int8 weight-only path is correctness-gated on the per-channel scale: the correct scale
passes, a wrong per-channel scale fails decisively (cosine 0.888 / rel 3.0 / pcc 0.888, all
three below the relaxed quant thresholds). Scale correctness IS tested. This is the negative
sibling of reports/w8_quant.log (happy path).
